    ('transportation-priorities', 3, 'Feb 3, 2026 — voted yes (named, 5-0) on Res 2910 authorizing grant applications for two transit projects and committing $175,000 in transit transportation impact fee funds as the required local match. 2024 campaign priority: "improved transportation infrastructure and walkability." Supports selective transit/pedestrian investment; no evidence of a road-capacity-first or transit-first-citywide position. Matches Chair 3 (maintain roads while selectively adding transit connections and pedestrian improvements).', ARRAY['https://hillsboro-oregon.civicweb.net/document/256729/City%20Council%20-%2003%20Feb%202026.pdf', 'https://hillsboronewstimes.com/2024/08/23/ward-3-profile-rob-harris-seeks-a-spot-on-hillsboro-city-council/']::text[]),
    ('homelessness-response', 3, '2024 Vote411/LWV questionnaire answer (first-party campaign statement): "City employees who have regular contact with homeless campers should be trained to assist with referring to resources such as housing, food and healthcare and to be educated on some forms of constructive behavior modification prompts." Campaign priorities included "homeless intervention programs." Service-referral/outreach orientation combined with pragmatic behavior management of campers in public space; no evidence for housing-first-no-enforcement or enforcement-first. Matches Chair 3 (invest in outreach, shelter, and mental health services while enforcing basic public-space rules).', ARRAY['https://onyourballot.vote411.org/race-detail.do?id=68912016']::text[]),
    ('growth-and-development', 3, 'Dec 2, 2025 — Harris personally MOVED first readings of Ord 6509 (Comprehensive Plan Amendment incorporating the Public Facilities Plan/system master plans — infrastructure planning ahead of growth) and Ord 6510 (adopting Metro 2040 Growth Concept regional & town center boundaries), both carrying 4-0 with Harris named yes. Consistent with his data-center pause rationale — "evaluate land use within current boundaries" before approving further expansion — and his urban-planning background. Managed, plan-first growth posture rather than growth caps or deregulation. Matches Chair 3 (plan proactively — invest in infrastructure ahead of growth to support responsible expansion).', ARRAY['https://hillsboro-oregon.civicweb.net/document/254837/City%20Council%20-%2002%20Dec%202025.pdf', 'https://www.grantspasstribune.com/hillsboro-weighs-temporary-halt-on-data-centers-as-oregon-reexamines-energy-costs-and-growth/']::text[])
